# Keep every text file LF in the working tree on every platform.
# Without this, Windows checkouts get CRLF (core.autocrlf=true is the Git-for-Windows
# default), which silently breaks the source-slicing tests in tests/ — their end
# markers contain "\n\n" and can never match "\r\n\r\n" — and inflates the raw-byte
# size budgets in tests/performance.test.mjs by ~1 byte per line.
* text=auto eol=lf

*.png  binary
*.webp binary
*.woff2 binary
*.ico  binary
*.jpg  binary
*.jpeg binary
